{
  "definition": "D2",
  "title": "WebAssembly feature / proposal list",
  "dataVersion": "2.1.0",
  "sha256": "81bc142b27ec9de4a9cd87644c4bbc405ad6cc4d1aa1ce0cef7712e1184a5ad9",
  "rules": {
    "name": "The canonical name: the key of binaryang's `Features` (`allFeatures()`, `defaultFeatures()`).",
    "cli": "The spelling binaryang's CLIs accept, as `--enable-<cli>` / `--disable-<cli>` — upstream wabt's and wasm-tools'.",
    "defaultOn": "On in `defaultFeatures()` (wabt's tool defaults; not the same as 'in Wasm 3.0').",
    "implemented": "false: the flag exists and changes nothing (see `note`).",
    "requires": "The features its proposal states it builds on — function-references 'is based on the reference types proposal'; GC: reference types and typed function references, 'Both proposals are prerequisites'; custom descriptors is 'for WasmGC structs' (its title); relaxed SIMD's every instruction takes `v128`, which only SIMD defines. RECORDED, NOT ENFORCED (owner, 2026-10-24): nothing turns a feature on or off with another and no feature set is refused; each instruction is gated by its own D1 `feature`. So with functionReferences off and gc on, `call_ref` is refused and a GC struct is accepted — as wasmtime 50 and wasm-tools 1.262 do.",
    "presets": "Named feature sets: exactly these on, every other off. wasm1, wasm2, wasm3 are the specification's releases (its change history, document/core/appendix/changes.rst; mutableGlobals predates it, so it is in 1.0); all is every feature. wasm2 is `defaultOn`.",
    "testsuiteDirs": "Directories of the spec testsuite (relative to its root) whose suites need this feature. Empty: its tests are in the core suite, which runs with every feature on except as `onlyIn` / `offIn` say.",
    "onlyIn": "Absent: on everywhere. Present: ON only in these directories — it CHANGES core semantics, and the core suite (or another) asserts against the change.",
    "offIn": "Directories whose suite must run with this feature OFF — a snapshot written before the feature, which it relaxes.",
    "since": "The date the entry entered this list."
  },
